    description: "STATEMENT: a call on a receiver whose type the file writes reaches a method the type gets by using a trait or mixin (PHP use T; in a class body), as it reaches one the type inherits. OBSERVED: php.py records no relation between a class and the traits it uses, so the hierarchy walk of inherited_calls does not visit them: $user->podcasts() on a typed User (which uses HasUserRelationships) is unresolved. On two PHP trees (koel, grpc src/php): 18 typed calls lost to this, and 93 of the 379 calls that were resolved before the batch and are not now had a trait method for target. Adding the relation changes inheritance edges, which batch 5a was not allowed to move. The same question is open for every language with mixins that a later batch moves (Ruby include, Scala with, Dart with).\n\nEvidence and method: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/batch5a_11262026/ (DESIGN.md; php_RESULTS.md, java_RESULTS.md, kotlin_RESULTS.md; maps mine_e566 on the batch branch against before/ at dev 619ebe7ac; blind judgments judge/judgments_<lang>.jsonl scored by judge/score.py, samples seed 20261125). Found during batch 5a of ADR-0064 (java, kotlin, php)."  # 3964
